{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they pressed the man, Lot</b> I have not found this expression except in the context of entreaty. If so, we explain it as follows: they importuned him greatly to open the door for them, and when he refused to do so, they approached to break it down. Or he was standing in front of the door and would not let them come near it, and they pleaded with him to step aside from before them, for they did not wish to strike him. And this is the meaning of \"Step aside, please\" (גֶּשׁ הָלְאָה) — that he should step aside to another place:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {0 "Ramban derives the meaning of ויפצרו from its only other biblical occurrence, in contexts of entreaty/persuasion (cf. Exodus 12:33, Jonah 3:8)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:31:48.503836231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}